{"title":"2024 SSMO Tiebreaker Round Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute the exact value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f1fcd95649c6c686de74e7e28c75168ac68303e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^2+0^2+2^2+4^2+20^2+22^2+24^2+40^2+42^2+202^2.\\]\" width=\"432\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 SSMO Tiebreaker Round Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bob is attempting to shoot a 3-point throw. Bob attempts the basket 97 times. Each time, Bob has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af59f5a81354c1925a58cb897e1d142111b1d7c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> chance of making the shot. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> denotes the expected number of points Bob will make and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4caea56d945d0b6e49701b42ce06e0fb92e663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> the number of points Bob is most likely to make, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43fe4c1dfea7013b5690522ae5f7124f5cca209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_1-S_2| = \\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 SSMO Tiebreaker Round Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/e/33ef94d7abd6485fcc63d65453dca21e3d77feaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\dots a_2a_1a_0.a_{-1}a_{-2}a_{-3}\\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" /> be a terminating decimal. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is defined to be the length of the shortest sub-sequence of consecutive digits that include all nonzero digits and at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/5/ad53c840b653eb8326147f9c67cc1421cf0496bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0,a_{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />. So, the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e03688c52bd22f82cd2a1b2cdd01ed65839befd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12.03$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa19a08fb70a01dcb44f3727778ef281ce663d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.123$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the average of all numbers with a terminating decimal of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1cf9f707b2c4ac3b4e5f448668d61fbeeec93b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\sum_{n=0}^{10}(n+1)f(n)\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"142\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 SSMO Tiebreaker Round Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232606\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 80/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3249/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31874:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232606 and revision id 277062. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}